# Help: KVM x86's optional parts: Hyper-V and Xen emulation, SEV, SGX, TDX
#
# Layered on virt/kvm-x86_64.config: the Hyper-V and Xen hypercall
# emulation, AMD SEV through the Secure Processor's PSP, SGX enclaves
# and Intel TDX for guests, and the code KVM runs when the host is
# itself a Hyper-V guest. Each defaults to y or follows a host option
# an allnoconfig-based merge leaves off, so a guest built from
# kvm-x86_64.config alone compiles none of arch/x86/kvm's hyperv.c,
# xen.c, svm/sev.c, vmx/sgx.c or vmx/tdx.c.
#
# Prerequisites inlined per the self-containment rule:
# - virt/kvm-x86_64.config's KVM with Intel and AMD.
# - HYPERVISOR_GUEST=y + HYPERV=y for the *_onhyperv.c files.
# - CRYPTO_DEV_CCP_DD with the PSP, on the AMD IOMMU, for KVM_AMD_SEV,
#   under CRYPTO and under CRYPTO_HW, whose default y an allnoconfig-based
#   merge drops; builtin/virt/kvm-extras-x86_64.config builds CCP in,
#   as a built-in KVM_AMD needs.
# - X86_SGX on X86_X2APIC for X86_SGX_KVM.
# - INTEL_TDX_HOST, on X86_MCE and the contiguous allocator (CMA), for
#   KVM_INTEL_TDX.
# See: arch/x86/kvm/Kconfig
# See: https://docs.kernel.org/virt/kvm/x86/index.html

#
# Inlined prerequisites
#
CONFIG_VIRTUALIZATION=y
CONFIG_KVM=m
CONFIG_KVM_INTEL=m
CONFIG_KVM_AMD=m
CONFIG_HYPERVISOR_GUEST=y
CONFIG_HYPERV=y
CONFIG_AMD_IOMMU=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO=m
CONFIG_CRYPTO_HW=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO_DEV_CCP=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO_DEV_CCP_DD=m
CONFIG_CRYPTO_DEV_SP_PSP=y
CONFIG_X86_X2APIC=y
CONFIG_X86_SGX=y
CONFIG_X86_MCE=y
CONFIG_CMA=y
CONFIG_INTEL_TDX_HOST=y

#
# KVM features
#
CONFIG_KVM_HYPERV=y
CONFIG_KVM_XEN=y
CONFIG_KVM_AMD_SEV=y
CONFIG_X86_SGX_KVM=y
CONFIG_KVM_INTEL_TDX=y
